// Rstest Snapshot v1

exports[`the main thread's catalogue > change_not_applied: the message 1`] = `
"A change to the page could not be applied on the main thread: The main thread has no element 7.
While trying to insert <view> 42 into <scroll-view> 7.

The rest of the change was applied. This is a bug in @sohedra/lynx: report it with the component and the steps that lead to it.
https://sohedra.com/e/change_not_applied"
`;

exports[`the main thread's catalogue > element_has_no_view: the message 1`] = `
"Lynx could not run boundingClientRect: the element has no view on the screen. Lynx makes a view only for an element it draws, not for one that is hidden or not shown yet.

Call boundingClientRect once the element is shown, for example after a layoutchange event of the element.
https://sohedra.com/e/element_has_no_view"
`;

exports[`the main thread's catalogue > element_left_page: the message 1`] = `
"Lynx could not run scrollTo: the element was removed from the page in the same update, before Lynx ran the call.

Call the method while the element is on the page, or check that it still is, for example in the attachment that keeps it.
https://sohedra.com/e/element_left_page"
`;

exports[`the main thread's catalogue > element_missing: the message 1`] = `
"The main thread has no element 7.

The two threads disagree about the page. This is a bug in @sohedra/lynx: report it with the component and the steps that lead to it.
https://sohedra.com/e/element_missing"
`;

exports[`the main thread's catalogue > element_released: the message 1`] = `
"A main-thread function called setStyleProperty on an element the page has let go of, so nothing happened.

Read the element where the function runs, from its event's target or a ref the element holds now, rather than keeping it past its element's life.
https://sohedra.com/e/element_released"
`;

exports[`the main thread's catalogue > first_frame_call_unanswered: the message 1`] = `
"A main-thread function called runOnBackground in the first frame, and no background function took the call when the background took the page over, so it has no answer (3 calls).

Call it from an element the background renders the same way as the first frame, not one inside {#if mainThread} or a branch the threads take apart, or once the page has started.
https://sohedra.com/e/first_frame_call_unanswered"
`;

exports[`the main thread's catalogue > first_frame_event_dropped: the message 1`] = `
"The first frame's tap or touchstart event on <text id="login" class="login"> was dropped, 2 times: the element is in a part of the page that may differ between the first frame and the page once it started, so no handler ran for it.

Render that part from the page's data, which both threads have, so the first frame draws what the background renders. A part only the background renders, such as {#if background}, and an {#await} given a promise, which the page draws again once it started, also drop the events heard before then in the {#if} blocks beside them, in the same element: give each an element of its own, as in <view>{#if background}…{/if}</view>. Events after the page has started are handled as usual.
https://sohedra.com/e/first_frame_event_dropped"
`;

exports[`the main thread's catalogue > first_frame_markup_unreadable: the message 1`] = `
"The first frame was not drawn: its markup could not be read at character 11, where the value of class on <view> is not quoted.

The page is shown when the background has made it. This is a bug in @sohedra/lynx: report it with the component and the steps that lead to it.
https://sohedra.com/e/first_frame_markup_unreadable"
`;

exports[`the main thread's catalogue > first_frame_threw: the message 1`] = `
"The first frame was not drawn: a component threw as the page rendered it on the main thread (NativeModules is not defined).

Keep code only the background can run, such as a native module or the background's lynx APIs, out of a component's top level: in an effect, an event handler, or in {#if background} from @sohedra/lynx/environment. The page is shown when the background has made it.
https://sohedra.com/e/first_frame_threw"
`;

exports[`the main thread's catalogue > lazy_bundle_not_on_main_thread: the message 1`] = `
"The lazy bundle https://cdn.example/lazy-bundle/Chart.bundle reached the background but not the main thread, so its main-thread functions and styles are missing.

Check that the bundle is served at that address and that the device reaches it: the main thread takes the bundle again only when the page is opened again.
https://sohedra.com/e/lazy_bundle_not_on_main_thread"
`;

exports[`the main thread's catalogue > list_row_not_written: the message 1`] = `
"A <list> asked for its row 12, which the page has not written, so the row stays empty.

The list's other rows are shown. This is a bug in @sohedra/lynx: report it with the component and the steps that lead to it.
https://sohedra.com/e/list_row_not_written"
`;

exports[`the main thread's catalogue > main_thread_attribute_unknown: the message 1`] = `
"The attribute main-thread:bindtap-later binds nothing: a main-thread attribute is main-thread:ref, main-thread:gesture or a main-thread event.

Write a main-thread event as main-thread:ontap, main-thread:ontapcapture, main-thread:oncatchtap or main-thread:oncatchtapcapture, with the event's name in place of tap.
https://sohedra.com/e/main_thread_attribute_unknown"
`;

exports[`the main thread's catalogue > main_thread_function_not_found: the message 1`] = `
"The main-thread function 9aef:c44c3:1 has no body on the main thread: the module that declares it did not load there.

A function of a bundle loaded with import() runs once that bundle has loaded. Otherwise, this is a bug in @sohedra/lynx: report it with the component and the steps that lead to it.
https://sohedra.com/e/main_thread_function_not_found"
`;

exports[`the main thread's catalogue > main_thread_update_loop: the message 1`] = `
"Main-thread functions changed the page 1000 times in a row, and the main thread got no turn for anything else: a main-thread function probably changes what makes it run again.
The last to run was 9aef:c44c3:2, for the event layoutchange.
Its last change was setStyleProperty(height).

Change the element only when the value differs, as a layout handler that sets a size or a scroll handler that sets a scroll position must. Until the main thread's next turn, what main-thread functions change is not shown.
https://sohedra.com/e/main_thread_update_loop"
`;

exports[`the main thread's catalogue > main_thread_value_not_runnable: the message 1`] = `
"Lynx asked the main thread to run a value that is not a main-thread function, so nothing ran.

The engine handed back something the page did not give it. This is a bug in @sohedra/lynx: report it with the component and the steps that lead to it.
https://sohedra.com/e/main_thread_value_not_runnable"
`;

exports[`the main thread's catalogue > main_thread_value_too_deep: the message 1`] = `
"A value a main-thread function captured or was given is nested more than 1000 levels deep, so the function did not run.

Give the function a flatter value, or only the part of it the function reads.
https://sohedra.com/e/main_thread_value_too_deep"
`;

exports[`the main thread's catalogue > not_a_background_function_handle: the message 1`] = `
"The value given to runOnBackground, save, is not a background function it can call, so the call has no answer.

Call runOnBackground(fn) in the body of a function that starts with 'main thread', with fn the background function itself: the build turns it into what the call needs there.
https://sohedra.com/e/not_a_background_function_handle"
`;

exports[`the main thread's catalogue > page_is_gone: the message 1`] = `
"A call of runOnBackground has no answer: the page it was made on has been closed or reloaded.

Nothing to fix when the page closed on purpose. Otherwise, stop the timers and animations of a page that reloads, so they make no calls for it.
https://sohedra.com/e/page_is_gone"
`;

exports[`the main thread's catalogue > rewrite_not_page: the message 1`] = `
"The background wrote element 7 again, and the main thread writes only the whole page again.

The rest of the change was applied. This is a bug in @sohedra/lynx: report it with the component and the steps that lead to it.
https://sohedra.com/e/rewrite_not_page"
`;

exports[`the main thread's catalogue > ui_method_failed: the message 1`] = `
"Lynx could not run setValue on the element: it answered with the code 4.

Check that the element is on the page, and that Lynx's docs list setValue as a UI method of its tag.
https://sohedra.com/e/ui_method_failed"
`;
